<title>UK: UK social security spend to rise 1.5 pct/yr-Clarke.</title>
<headline>UK social security spend to rise 1.5 pct/yr-Clarke.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chancellor of the Exchequer Kenneth Clarke said Britain's social security budget will grow by around 1.5 percent per year.</p>
<p>&quot;In recent budgets we have taken action to bring that growth (in social security spending) under control,&quot; Clarke told parliament in his annual budget speech.</p>
<p>&quot;We now expect future growth of 1.5 percent a year. Well below the growth of the economy.&quot;</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
